  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The RMT union has initiated a 24-hour strike involving London Underground drivers, leading to significant travel disruption across the city. Passengers have been advised to plan their journeys in advance due to the expected impact on transport services and a complete early shutdown of the network. The action has prompted a war of words between union officials and political figures, with RMT leadership publicly challenging the Mayor of London to address the underlying issues of the dispute. While the walkout caused broad service interruptions, some services, such as the Piccadilly line, reported that some staff continued to report for their shifts. The strike is expected to affect travel into Friday morning, as the network works toward returning to normal operations. Transport for London continues to provide passenger advice as the situation remains fluid across the various Tube lines.",
